## Original Content
Chinese President Xi Jinping and King of the Hashemite Kingdom of Jordan Abdullah II ibn Al Hussein attended a signing ceremony of cooperation documents in Beijing on Monday.

## Summary
Chinese President Xi Jinping and King Abdullah II of Jordan jointly attended a signing ceremony for cooperation documents in Beijing. The event marks continued diplomatic and cooperative relations between China and Jordan.

## Key Points
- Chinese President Xi Jinping and Jordan's King Abdullah II attended a joint signing ceremony.
- The ceremony was for cooperation documents between China and Jordan.
- The event took place in Beijing on a Monday.
- It signifies ongoing bilateral relations and cooperation.


